        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-17T10:50:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we disable pkvm_enabled_key without reprivileging, kernel will be confused about hypercalls as hypercalls are gated behind this static key. Without iommu, there are not much hypercalls, but we have IRQ_REMAP which still uses hypercalls now. So its safe to keep it enabled until we succeed in reprivileging",
      "parentUuid": "33f907b0_7055e9f8",
      "revId": "c237b9d9b7b0378ffd13f83dad3a85aa1c1ecee6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
