      "writtenOn": "2025-06-12T00:13:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why so intricate? And this actually seems incorrect: if __vmx_pkvm_init() failed but then pkvm_iommu_driver_init() succeeded, we return success?\n\nAgain, what\u0027s so special about pkvm_iommu_driver_prepare() and pkvm_iommu_driver_init() that we need to move the rest of vmx_pkvm_init() to a separate function?\n\nWhat\u0027s wrong with just adding these pkvm_iommu_driver_prepare() and pkvm_iommu_driver_init() calls to the appropriate places in the existing vmx_pkvm_init() and let it handle pkvm_iommu_driver_init() failure (almost) like other failures?",
      "revId": "c237b9d9b7b0378ffd13f83dad3a85aa1c1ecee6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
